                  <additions>
                     <list>
                        <item xml:id="a1">
                           <locus target="#1r"/>
                           <desc>List of tributes or register of land parcels (?).  It lists some revenues (mostly honeycombs) from lands followed by the names of individuals who paid them. 
                              The note is written in a mediocre but careful hand. Some parts are illegible due to faded ink.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="ti">ኍልቆ፡ እርሻ፡ ዘባን፡ ጨአ፡ ፩ገራ፡ ክፉእ፡ ወድቅጽው፡ ፩ገራብ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a2">
                           <locus from="2r" to="2v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">Excerpt from <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2278salota">Second Prayer of Moses</title> and <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2703salota">The Third Prayer of Moses</title>.  They are written in <ref target="h1">Hand 1</ref>.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a3">
                           <locus target="#140r"/>
                           <desc type="DonationNote">The note states that <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15310WalattaTakHay">Walatta Takla Hāymānot</persName> and her mother <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15307AmataMikael">ʾAmata Mikāʾel</persName>
                              bought the manuscript and donated it to the church <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0174MAKM">Kidāna Mǝḥrat Māy ʾAnbasā</placeName>. 
                              It also mentions their spiritual fathers. Two other spiritual (?) fathers are mentioned above the note. The note is written in red ink by the same secondary hand as that in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESmakm002#a2">Ms. MAKM-002, Additio 2</ref>. 
                              These individuals are also mentioned in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESmakm002#a2">Ms. MAKM-002, Additio 2</ref>.
                              The handwriting is mediocre, characterized by angular letters. <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15310WalattaTakHay">Walatta Takla Hāymānot</persName> and her sister <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15309SabanaGiyorgis">Sabana Giyorgis</persName> appear in a brief supplication written at the top of the donation note by another
                              secondary hand. The note is separated from the main text by chains of black and red dots, with nine-dot asterisks in between.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"><hi rend="rubric">ዝመፅሐፍ፡ ዘወለተ፡ ተክለ፡ ሃይማኖት፡ አመተ፡ ሚካኤል: ዘተሳየጠት፡ በወርቅ። ወሃበታ፡ ለኪዳነ፡ ምረት፡  ዘማየ<sic/>፡ አንበሳ። ወአቡሐ፡ አቡነ፡ ገብረ፡ 
                              ስላሴ፡ ወእማ፡ እግዚ፡ ሐረያ፡ አቡነ፡ ገብረ፡ ሚካኤል፡ አቡነ፡ ተክለ፡ ሚካኤል።<add place="above">አቡነ፡ ወልደ፡ ስላሴ፡ አቡነ፡ ገብረ፡ ማርያም፡</add>
                              <add place="above">መሐረኒ፡ ወተሣሃለኒ፡ ለዓመትከ፡ ሰበነ፡ ጊዮርጊስ፡ ወለተ፡ተክለ፡ ሃይማኖት፡</add></hi></q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e1">
                           <desc>The title, <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዳዊት</foreign>, is written on the front board with blue paint.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e2">
                           <locus target="#85r"/>
                           <desc>Shelfmark C4-IV-65</desc> 
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e3">
                           <desc>The Psalms are divided into groups of 10 by means of a chain of red and black dots.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e4">
                           <locus target="#3r #3v #4r #4v #5r #5v #6v #7v #9v #10v"/>
                          <desc type="Directive">Numerous directives on use of the
                           Psalms for protective and medical purposes are written in the margin and
                           beside the main text, in a fine hand and with smaller letters.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e5">
                           <locus target="#4v #9r #15r #52r #122r #146v #149r #162v"/>
                           <desc>The scribe reduced the size of his handwriting to accommodate the end of
                              the line. The folia listed above are a few examples.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e6">
                           <locus target="#4v #9v #13v #28v #29v #32v #46v #78v #87v #132r #141v"/>
                           <desc>Part of the line is taken up.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e7">
                           <locus target="#177v13"/>
                           <desc type="Correction">Tamallas-sign, in the shape of a cross, indicating the place where the
                              omitted verse of  <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>, written in the upper margin, belongs.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e8">
                           <locus target="#8v #9r #50r #96v #106r #108r #109v #117r #129r #131v #157r #161r #168r"/>
                           <desc type="Correction">Many omissions or corrections are written interlineally or as a continuation of the
                           preceding verse. The folia listed above are a few examples.</desc>
                           </item>
                        <item xml:id="e9">
                           <locus target="#7v #9r #9v #39r #98v #142r #147v"/>
                           <desc type="Correction">Corrections written over erased words and passages. The folia listed above are a few examples.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e10">
                           <locus target="#26v #33v #53r #69v #102v #124r"/>
                           <desc type="Correction">Erasures. The folia listed above are a few examples.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e11">
                           <locus target="#164v"/>
                           <desc type="StampExlibris">Two stamps of the owning institution (?), barely legible.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e12">
                           <locus target="#1v #36r"/>
                           <desc>Pen trial.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e13">
                           <locus target="#1r #1v #2r #31v #32r #63r #168v"/>
                           <desc>Scribbles and doodles.</desc>
                        </item>
                     </list>
                  </additions>
                  
                  <bindingDesc>
                     <binding contemporary="partly">
                        <decoNote xml:id="b1">Two wooden boards.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b2" type="Cover">The leather cover is for the most part missing; remnants of turn-ins and <term key="textileInlay" ana="#textileInlay">textile inlays</term> are visible on the
                           inner side of the back board.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b3" type="Sewing">Two pairs of sewing stations.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b4" type="SewingStations">4</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b5" type="bindingMaterial">
                           <material key="wood"/>
                           <material key="leather"/>
                        </decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b6" type="Endbands">Missing.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b7" type="Other">Small holes are visible on the spine fold
                           of the quires, two close to the head and two close to the tail of the codex.</decoNote>
                     </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
               </physDesc>
