                     </origPlace>
                     <origDate notBefore="1800" notAfter="1899">19th century (?).</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance><persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15310WalattaTakHay">Walatta Takla Hāymānot</persName> and <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15307AmataMikael">ʾAmata Mikāʾel</persName> are
                     mentioned as donors in <ref target="#a3"/>. Both of them and their family members appear in  supplication formulas written by a secondary hand, in red, on
                     <locus target="#10r #18v #27r #38r #47r #53v #63v #76v #86r #92v #107v #122r #125v #133r #140r"/>. Names of some other individuals are written
                     below the names of the donor and her family members, in another secondary hand,
                     in black ink. The same individuals who appear in this manuscript are also mentioned in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESmakm002">ʾƎndartā, Māy ʾAnbasā Dabra Gannat Kidāna Mǝḥrat, C4-IV-9</ref>.</provenance></history>
